WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.120 --> 00:00:02.449
Hey guys, it's Jan here.

00:00:02.449 --> 00:00:07.580
As I said in my review, I was seriously impressed
with Season 2 of Marvel's Daredevil on Netflix.

00:00:07.580 --> 00:00:12.349
Not only are there some great new characters
on board this year, but it's also absolutely

00:00:12.349 --> 00:00:15.910
jam-packed with shocking, heart-in-your-mouth
moments.

00:00:15.910 --> 00:00:20.330
So, I wanted to look back over the most WTF
moments in this video.

00:00:20.330 --> 00:00:24.270
Just before I kick off, I've got an awesome
giveaway from our friends at Entertainment

00:00:24.270 --> 00:00:25.270
Earth.

00:00:25.270 --> 00:00:29.090
For a chance to win this exclusive cool pair
of Marvel collectibles, a Thanos Infinity

00:00:29.090 --> 00:00:33.989
Gauntlet Mug and Punisher's Dog Tags, make
sure you subscribe and comment about your

00:00:33.989 --> 00:00:36.929
favourite moment in season 2 on this video.

00:00:36.929 --> 00:00:40.989
For more details and ways to enter the giveaway,
check out the Gleam link in the video description

00:00:40.989 --> 00:00:44.780
below and also the links to the prizes on
Entertainment Earth!

00:00:44.780 --> 00:00:48.789
Obviously, spoilers ahead if you haven't watched
the whole of season 2 already!

00:00:48.789 --> 00:00:52.179
And if that's you, I've got a non-spoiler
review for you right here.

00:00:52.179 --> 00:00:56.809
In the final episode, after battling ninjas,
literally getting pulled through a wall, and

00:00:56.809 --> 00:01:02.890
having a heart-to-heart with Matt, Elektra
faces off a barrage of katana-and-longbow-wielding

00:01:02.890 --> 00:01:04.780
ninjas on the roof with Daredevil.

00:01:04.780 --> 00:01:08.940
During the fight, Nobu hits Daredevil so hard
that he knocks his mask off and is about to

00:01:08.940 --> 00:01:13.590
kill him when he ends up stabbing Elektra
instead as she tries to save Daredevil!

00:01:13.590 --> 00:01:18.010
'I know now what it feels to be good [...] This
is not the end,' she tells Matt.

00:01:18.010 --> 00:01:21.360
And just when we thought the final episode
was over with Matt's reveal of his Daredevil

00:01:21.360 --> 00:01:24.940
identity to Karen, the camera cuts to Elektra's
open grave.

00:01:24.940 --> 00:01:29.240
And then we see Elektra, who's dressed in
red silk similar to her comic book costume,

00:01:29.240 --> 00:01:31.160
being sealed in the Hand's sarcophagus.

00:01:31.160 --> 00:01:35.470
I can't wait to see how The Hand resurrect
her for next season!

00:01:35.470 --> 00:01:40.180
There's a fantastic fight sequence that makes
good use of confined spaces in episode 12.

00:01:40.180 --> 00:01:44.640
But the fight isn't the only reason this sequence
earns its WTF status.

00:01:44.640 --> 00:01:49.880
It all starts with a beautiful shot of Daredevil
inching down into the sewers, where he jumps

00:01:49.880 --> 00:01:53.600
to the ground in a superhero landing pose
before walking through the tunnel towards

00:01:53.600 --> 00:01:54.600
the camera.

00:01:54.600 --> 00:01:58.980
It's not until he hears a sword swish, that
he realises he's been surrounded by ninjas;

00:01:58.980 --> 00:02:03.840
but he gets disoriented and can't use his
radar sense when they drop their weapons.

00:02:03.840 --> 00:02:08.500
And after climbing up a ladder from the tunnels,
he flails about when he's attacked by yet

00:02:08.500 --> 00:02:09.500
more ninjas.

00:02:09.500 --> 00:02:14.220
That is, until he hears Stick, who's been
captured by the Hand and held nearby.

00:02:14.220 --> 00:02:18.390
Stick tells Daredevil to track the ninjas'
breath and as soon as he does that, he wipes

00:02:18.390 --> 00:02:20.410
the floor with their ninja asses!

00:02:20.410 --> 00:02:21.939
But that's not the end of it!

00:02:21.939 --> 00:02:25.720
Daredevil confronts the men torturing Stick,
who takes a bloody piece out of one of his

00:02:25.720 --> 00:02:26.720
captors' ears!

00:02:26.720 --> 00:02:30.290
Then Elektra arrives to kill Stick for trying
to have her killed!

00:02:30.290 --> 00:02:34.909
And Nobu turns up with more ninjas to reveal
that Elektra is actually the mysterious Black

00:02:34.909 --> 00:02:38.090
Sky, in other words the Hand's greatest living
weapon!

00:02:38.090 --> 00:02:39.090
Daredevil persuades Elektra to reject the
Hand, and instead she puts her signature sai

00:02:39.090 --> 00:02:40.090
blades to use helping Stick escape.

00:02:40.090 --> 00:02:41.090
Meanwhile Daredevil fights off more ninjas
and kicks Nobu flying over a railing, although

00:02:41.090 --> 00:02:42.090
that's not quite enough to put an end to the
ninja with nine lives!

00:02:42.090 --> 00:02:43.209
After Daredevil and Punisher's roof-top brawl
in episode 1, which saw Frank Castle bring

00:02:43.209 --> 00:02:48.040
a gun to a fist-and-foot fight, it wasn't
long before the two men were at it again.

00:02:48.040 --> 00:02:52.599
Episode 2 saw the Man without Fear face off
with Castle once more, only this time, they

00:02:52.599 --> 00:02:56.989
had a leaky water tower raining down on them
and a hail of bullets from police who'd set

00:02:56.989 --> 00:02:58.349
a trap for Castle.

00:02:58.349 --> 00:03:02.760
But ending that battle chained up after falling
through a glass ceiling was just the beginning

00:03:02.760 --> 00:03:04.069
of Daredevil's problems.

00:03:04.069 --> 00:03:08.730
Yes, after discussing ethics and facing Castle's
moral conundrum, Daredevil had to contend

00:03:08.730 --> 00:03:13.459
with a hoard of angry bikers on the rampage
after Castle blew up their bikes.

00:03:13.459 --> 00:03:17.540
Let's just say those chains he'd been tied
up in actually came in rather handy as Daredevil

00:03:17.540 --> 00:03:22.769
brawled his way through one Dogs of Hell biker
after another down a long corridor and flight

00:03:22.769 --> 00:03:26.999
of stairs, kicking, punching, running up walls,
and back-flipping his way out of danger.

00:03:26.999 --> 00:03:32.370
This whole sequence was incredibly choreographed,
acted, and shot, from Daredevil's down-and-dirty

00:03:32.370 --> 00:03:36.849
brawling mixed with martial arts influences,
to his smashing the ceiling lights with his

00:03:36.849 --> 00:03:40.879
chain, to the red light that drenched the
second part of the scene, and Daredevil taking

00:03:40.879 --> 00:03:44.849
a moment to stretch his neck before starting
his second ass-kicking session.

00:03:44.849 --> 00:03:49.310
Clearly, the intention was to up the ante
from the already amazing corridor fight we

00:03:49.310 --> 00:03:53.300
saw in season 1, which was an homage to the
movie Oldboy.

00:03:53.300 --> 00:03:57.080
Although Wilson Fisk wasn't in trailers for
Season 2, I had a sneaky suspicion that he'd

00:03:57.080 --> 00:03:58.650
be making a comeback this year.

00:03:58.650 --> 00:04:03.519
So, I was delighted when he popped up right
at the end of Episode 8 to tell new prison

00:04:03.519 --> 00:04:06.790
inmate Frank Castle, 'I see you got my message'.

00:04:06.790 --> 00:04:11.480
Such a simple line, yet so loaded with meaning
about the nature and extent of Fisk's power,

00:04:11.480 --> 00:04:13.209
even when he's incarcerated.

00:04:13.209 --> 00:04:17.799
At that point, he was already running one
of the prison guards and, with Castle's help,

00:04:17.799 --> 00:04:23.520
he soon became the new prison kingpin, enjoying
red wine, steak, and a flat-screen TV in his

00:04:23.520 --> 00:04:24.520
cell.

00:04:24.520 --> 00:04:29.000
I loved Vincent D'Onofrio's nicely understated
turn as the shadowy Fisk in Season 1, and

00:04:29.000 --> 00:04:32.621
he certainly brought the brilliance again
this season, making sure we knew that, with

00:04:32.621 --> 00:04:38.129
Fisk, danger is ever-present, no matter how
softly spoken or cultured he appears.

00:04:38.129 --> 00:04:41.830
During the exchange between Fisk and fellow
prisoner Dutton, who lays down the law, in

00:04:41.830 --> 00:04:46.160
episode 9, you just knew Dutton was already
living on borrowed time.

00:04:46.160 --> 00:04:50.310
And what about when Matt Murdoch goes to see
Fisk in prison to confront him about Frank

00:04:50.310 --> 00:04:51.830
Castle's escape?

00:04:51.830 --> 00:04:57.070
Fisk goes from restrained to caged beast in
a matter of minutes when Murdoch threatens

00:04:57.070 --> 00:05:00.770
to make sure Fisk never sees his beloved Vanessa
again.

00:05:00.770 --> 00:05:05.181
Frank Castle didn't realise quite what he
was getting himself in to with Fisk when he

00:05:05.181 --> 00:05:10.000
agreed to off the prison big-shot Dutton,
who facilitated the Central Park deal between

00:05:10.000 --> 00:05:15.340
the Dogs of Hell, Irish Mob, and Mexican Cartel
during which Castle's family was wiped out.

00:05:15.340 --> 00:05:19.710
After taking out Dutton's right-hand man,
Castle puts his shiv to use dragging the truth

00:05:19.710 --> 00:05:24.409
out of Dutton about what went down that fateful
day, including details about the involvement

00:05:24.409 --> 00:05:28.900
of undercover cops and the Blacksmith, a shadowy
new player in the drug trade.

00:05:28.900 --> 00:05:33.750
But it's what happens after this that makes
this scene a true WTF moment.

00:05:33.750 --> 00:05:38.360
When Castle tries to exit Dutton's cell block
after killing him, the prison guards on Fisk's

00:05:38.360 --> 00:05:44.509
payroll won't let him out; instead, they open
the cell doors so Dutton's men can kill Castle!

00:05:44.509 --> 00:05:49.319
Cue Castle slashing, stabbing, stamping, and
pummelling his way through a pack of enraged

00:05:49.319 --> 00:05:54.130
and armed prisoners until he's the last man
standing and his face, arms, and white prison

00:05:54.130 --> 00:05:56.360
uniform are soaked in blood.

00:05:56.360 --> 00:06:01.169
It's an especially savage scene which showcases
Castle's brutal, no-holds-barred fighting

00:06:01.169 --> 00:06:02.360
style to great effect.

00:06:02.360 --> 00:06:06.520
And, of course, it all happens in a narrow
corridor, something that's fast becoming a

00:06:06.520 --> 00:06:08.610
signature of the show's action scenes.

00:06:08.610 --> 00:06:13.080
Of course, there were loads of other crazy
moments this season too, including the Irish

00:06:13.080 --> 00:06:18.210
mob boss Finn stabbing one of his associates
in the eye and torturing Castle, the creepy

00:06:18.210 --> 00:06:22.699
children being tapped for their blood, the
big ninja fight at the hospital, the sequence

00:06:22.699 --> 00:06:24.750
at the Yakatomi building, and tons more!

00:06:24.750 --> 00:06:29.449
Now, what are the moments that shocked you
most in Season 2 of Daredevil?

